description:
Design a clock gating circuit that controls the clock signal based on an enable signal (EN) and a test enable signal (TE). When EN is asserted, the circuit captures the TE state on the rising edge of the CLK and propagates it to create the output ENCLK, which is a delayed version of TE. This output can effectively enable or disable clock signals to downstream components, reducing power consumption during idle states.
module top_module(
  input CLK, EN, TE,
  output ENCLK
);

code:
module top_module(
  input CLK, EN, TE,
  output ENCLK
);reg ENCLK_reg1;
  reg ENCLK_reg2;

  always @ (posedge CLK) begin
    if (EN) begin
      ENCLK_reg1 <= TE;
      ENCLK_reg2 <= ENCLK_reg1;
    end
  end

  assign ENCLK = ENCLK_reg2;

endmodule

