description:
Design a 4-bit synchronous counter with asynchronous reset functionality. The counter increments its output value on each clock pulse, wrapping around after reaching the maximum value of 15 (4'b1111). When the reset signal is asserted, the counter output resets to zero. The design utilizes a series of D flip-flops (dffr_async_ns) to store the current state and transition to the next state based on the clock and reset signals, ensuring reliable state updates in synchronous operation.
module top_module(
    input clk,      // clock input
    input rst,      // asynchronous reset input
    output reg [3:0] q   // 4-bit output
);

code:
module top_module(
    input clk,      // clock input
    input rst,      // asynchronous reset input
    output reg [3:0] q   // 4-bit output
);reg [3:0] q_next; // Change from wire to reg since we are assigning values in always block

// ** Assume that dffr_async_ns is a registered D flip-flop with reset
// This section is removed, as the implementation of dffr_async_ns is not provided.
// If it were to be implemented separately, it would be declared here.

// assign the next state of the counter
always @ (posedge clk or posedge rst) begin
    if (rst) begin
        q_next <= 4'b0000;
    end else begin
        q_next <= q + 1;
    end
end

// assign the output of the counter
always @ (posedge clk or posedge rst) begin
    if (rst) begin
        q <= 4'b0000;
    end else begin
        q <= q_next;
    end
end

endmodule

