Design a 4-to-1 multiplexer using NAND gates. The module takes a 4-bit input vector A and a 2-bit select signal S. Based on the value of S, it routes one of the four input lines to the output using NAND logical operations. The output will be LOW when the selected input is HIGH, effectively inverting the standard operation of a multiplexer. The logic is managed through multiple levels of NAND gate configurations to ensure the desired signal is correctly selected and outputted.
