Design a 6-bit equality comparator. The module takes two 6-bit inputs, `a` and `b`, and outputs a single signal, `equal`, that indicates whether the two inputs are equal. The comparison is performed by checking each corresponding bit of the two inputs; if all bits are identical, the output is HIGH, otherwise it is LOW.
