Design a clock generator module that produces a 50 MHz output clock (clk_50m) based on an input clock signal (clk_in). The output clock toggles its state with each rising edge of the input clock, and it is reset to a low state when the resetn signal is deactivated. Additionally, the module indicates a locked state (output locked) that signals when the output clock is stable and operational, which is also held low during a reset condition.
